  "reviews": [
    {
      "game": "WitchSpring R",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/15138/450x258/witchspring-r-pc-game-steam-cover.jpg?v=1786971600",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/15138-buy-witchspring-r-pc-game-steam/",
      "user": "Clayn",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/themes/igv2/images/avatar2.svg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "One of the most underrated gems of game in general and especially in the jrpg market. \n\nThe story is written so well, far off the usual cliché stuffed \"friendship against evil\" themes of most of those rpgs. The story starts off silly and cutesy and evolves from every chapter constantly to a mature story with heavy themes and still keeps it lighthearted where it needs to be.\n\n\n\nA fun turn based Rpg with cool creature collecting and a light spell crafting mechanic to tinker around a little for customization.\n\n\n\nI would love to play all the other titles, but they are all mobile exclusive and dont exist anymore. Are you fricking kidding me?"
    },
    {
      "game": "Outriders",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/4835/450x258/outriders-pc-game-steam-cover.jpg?v=1786971600",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/4835-buy-outriders-pc-game-steam/",
      "user": "Beerfreak",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/themes/igv2/images/avatar2.svg",
      "sentiment": "dislike",
      "content": "Avoid this broken mess\n\n\n\nEven with everything gutted to Low, the game still collapses below 30 FPS during combat on my GTX 1060. For a fast-paced shooter, that’s completely unacceptable.\n\n\n\nAnd then there’s the forced always-online requirement for a supposedly single-player campaign. Your internet connection is part of the fucking game whether you want it or not. A connection hiccup can kick you out of the experience, because apparently a solo campaign wasn’t allowed to simply work offline.\n\n\n\nThe combat is merely decent, the story is painfully generic, and the technical state makes even that mediocre experience miserable.\n\n\n\nDon’t waste your money on this garbage. Not even for €10. Not even for €5. If you want a functional single-player sci-fi shooter, look elsewhere."
    },
    {
      "game": "Splasher",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/1939/450x258/splasher-pc-mac-game-steam-cover.jpg?v=1786971600",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/1939-buy-splasher-pc-mac-game-steam/",
      "user": "SpencerFs",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/avatars/31340590-1786905897.jpg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "Pretty fun game, I've only spent a few hours on it so far, if you like a good challenging platformer you should play this game. It's the right balance in between too hard and baby mode, nice indie game and for only $1.50 right now."
    },
    {
      "game": "Dragon's Dogma 2",
      "game_image": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/products/7911/450x258/dragon-s-dogma-2-pc-game-steam-europe-cover.jpg?v=1786971600",
      "game_url": "https://www.instant-gaming.com/en/7911-buy-dragon-s-dogma-2-pc-game-steam-europe/",
      "user": "KaimanElite111",
      "avatar": "https://gaming-cdn.com/images/avatars/27985206-1748170881.jpg",
      "sentiment": "like",
      "content": "I really enjoyed the combat, which is fun and engaging. The story can feel repetitive with constant back-and-forth errands, and traveling the roads may become tedious. Still, the spells are great. Overall, a solid 6/10."
    }
